  "title": "packet-frame: Fix NULL pointer dereference in color filter display",
  "description": "The MR fixes a NULL pointer dereference crash that was added with MR !23650.\n\n## Bug reproducer\n\n### Files\nI've managed to reproduce the issue with a bunch of PCAP I have, so I'm just providing the simplest PCAP to reproduce it: [beacon_mld_capa.pcap](/uploads/70a361bbee5afc0ea18e2bce4371310d/beacon_mld_capa.pcap)\n\nI used the following coloring rules: [colorfilters](/uploads/9953dd9e4b1f9b23ed01b6d7f547cc09/colorfilters)\n\n### Steps\n1. open the provided PCAP with Wireshark master (e96313f7e464bf3edec4c18c958d48ff7e6ee7c3)\n2. open dialog `View > Coloring Rules...`\n3. modify rule `Checksum errors` from `wlan.fcs.status == \"Bad\" || radiotap.flags.badfcs == True` to `wlan.fcs.status == \"Bad\" || radiotap.flags.badfcs == False`\n4. click on `OK`\n5. re-open dialog `View > Coloring Rules...`\n6. modify rule `Checksum errors` from `wlan.fcs.status == \"Bad\" || radiotap.flags.badfcs == False` to `wlan.fcs.status == \"Bad\" || radiotap.flags.badfcs == True`\n7. click on `OK`\n8. Crash: `'wireshark' terminated by signal SIGSEGV (Address boundary error)`\n\nAI-Assisted: yes [OpenCode(Qwen3.5)]",
  "state": "closed",
