        {
          "id": 3287827113,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "sorry guys and thanks for taking the time to find these issues. I've been looking into this, I submitted https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/24629, has_color_info is dropped entirely, as you suggested. Each conditionnow guards itself directly on color_filter.\n\n  The approach is different than this MR(setting color_filter from the first list entry) because I found another issue in this approach: it would display a paused filter in the single-filter fallback branch without a \\[PAUSED\\] label, making it look like an active primary rule.\n\n  I Also fixed a related stale proto_data bug found during testing, when a rule change causes a packet to stop matching, the old match list was only cleared if new matches were found, leaving stale filter text in Frame Details until a manual reload. Fixed by always clearing on re-colorized",
